# Time flies when ya having fun!

Time flies when ya having fun! Its June already zoom zoom boom ba da boom! This month we have the last of our classes for term two of this year, some holiday action fun for the kids and some exciting dancing news. Its been a fabulous month with lots of workshops and performances for little ones, big ones, school fairs and Fun Runs for Rhythm Culture clients. We love our PLAY! And of course we had our own series of events with the very first [Saturplay](/saturplay-stories-pics-highlights/) and the beginning of the new dance class in Palmwoods on Saturdays. Last week we even managed to meet with the Maleny Rotary Club for a Rhythm Culture information speech and we had no idea how many missions these guys are on! Very inspiring and it got our minds ticking about future projects that we would like to see underway in Africa. For the month of July, there are some brand new times for a couple of our classes and the Tuesday night dancing returns! Be sure to take note of the new classes starting July 14th. The African Childrens Choir is this weekend so make sure you grab you r tickets quick as lots of their shows have sold out. For the holidays in July we will be opening a few more spots for our private tuition sessions, so if you would like to treat yourself to some extra tuition in the holidays, contact us to book a spot. We hope you have a lovely month and see you all soon! ![](/media/2015/06/First-Last-Saturplay-30515-145-1.jpg)
